<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hundred Years' War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1337–1453</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hundred Years' War was a series of conflicts between the kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> from 1337 to 1453, caused by disputes over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gascony">Gascony</a> and English claims to the French crown. English victories at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-crecy">Crécy</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Poitiers</a> and Agincourt were reversed after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joan-of-arc">Joan of Arc</a>'s intervention in 1429. The war ended with the French victory at Castillon and the loss of Gascony to England.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hundred-years-war.jpg" alt="Hundred Years' War" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Schlacht_von_Azincourt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
